1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:05,000
It is an ancient technology that carries an explosive power.

2
00:00:05,001 --> 00:00:12,000
A simple mixture of sulfur, saltpeter, and charcoal, gunpowder has fueled wars for centuries.

3
00:00:12,001 --> 00:00:19,000
And despite the high-tech advances in modern warfare, it is still the primary persuader among soldiers in combat.

4
00:00:19,001 --> 00:00:23,000
Now, High Explosives on Modern Marvels.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,520
Camp Pendleton, California.

6
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,820
Here young Marines hone the skills critical to success on the battlefield.

7
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:48,075
Many train for missions we've come to recognize as the role of the U.S.

8
00:00:48,076 --> 00:00:48,776
Marine Corps.

9
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:57,880
But others train for a different mission, one far less familiar but equally as vital.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:14,000
1st Platoon Charlie Company.

11
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:21,540
These are the first combat engineers of the U.S. Marine Corps.

12
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:25,740
Like any Marine, their job is to defend freedom at a moment's notice.

13
00:01:25,741 --> 00:01:31,220
But unlike their brothers who use high-tech weaponry to deliver the deadly blow of high explosives,

14
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:36,820
these men face a more immediate task, the application of explosives by hand.

15
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:44,440
Their job? Blow the bridge, trench the road, or mine the field.

16
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:49,120
On this bottom fuselage right here, for anti-handling device...

17
00:01:49,121 --> 00:01:51,580
Basically what we do, depending on what unit you're in,

18
00:01:51,581 --> 00:01:55,200
your construction work and demolition work.

19
00:01:55,201 --> 00:02:01,160
You work with building land fortifications as far as obstacles.

20
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:08,420
And then demolition work is working with explosives, blowing up things.

21
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:11,700
A lot of times, if you're lucky, you get to build something and blow it up.

22
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:18,520
The combat engineer's job is to be as complete and diverse a Marine

23
00:02:18,521 --> 00:02:20,080
as the battlefield can utilize.

24
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:29,760
In addition to the traditional skills of warfare, they must handle tricky and delicate explosive devices.

25
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:33,860
They are expected to be the first in and the last out of a fight.

26
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:37,520
They must be cool under fire and have nerves of steel.

27
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:44,480
And they are expected to handle sufficient explosives to stop an enemy platoon, or their own, if they are not careful.

28
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:58,620
When this detonates, this actually inverts with the heat and the energy.

29
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:00,620
What happens, it's like this.

30
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:03,680
When it detonates, it just blows straight down.

31
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:04,460
That's all it does.

32
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:07,700
And the heat and the energy, the force goes straight into the ground.

33
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:16,820
Today's high explosive carries complex chemical designations such as RDX, HBX1, and Tetral.

34
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:22,580
But most are basically nitrate-based compounds mixed with inert moderators to make them more stable.

35
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:27,420
They require a severe shock or detonation to unleash their immense power.

36
00:03:28,340 --> 00:03:32,760
The type of explosives that we use, there's a variety of them.

37
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,360
It depends on the job that we're going to do.

38
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:39,720
We use a plastic explosive called C4 used for breaching and cutting.

39
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:44,840
We use TNT for, like, pushing stumps, doing dirt removal.

40
00:03:44,841 --> 00:03:46,360
We're going to make tank ditches.

41
00:03:46,820 --> 00:03:52,480
We have mines that we use to stop and channelize vehicles and personnel.

42
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:59,160
Today, these Marines are rigging explosives on simulated targets.

43
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:05,780
Each device does a different job, but all are designed to assist the Marines in carrying out their combat duties.

44
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:11,020
When the fuses are set and the troops withdrawn, it is time to test their handiwork.

