and just chunk them full of all kinds of stuff,

108
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:47,060
everything we could put in there

109
00:08:47,061 --> 00:08:50,320
and make our own bombs,

110
00:08:50,980 --> 00:08:52,980
seal them up, put their fuse in,

111
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:58,200
We'd get over a road and we'd see a line of trucks.

112
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:06,820
So we'd try to work out our windage, and we'd let them go.

113
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:13,540
Then we'd fire them back, and we'd try to watch the trajectory as they dropped.

114
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:20,360
And sometimes we'd be 300 yards off target.

115
00:09:20,361 --> 00:09:23,020
after you did it maybe three or four times,

116
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:25,580
you got pretty good where you could come pretty close to it.

117
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:32,600
During World War I, bombs grew from 5 pounds to over 500,

118
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:36,700
