00:39:04,280 --> 00:39:09,140
Smart bombs are guided to their targets via a laser beam from the attacking aircraft.

461
00:39:10,380 --> 00:39:16,740
Correcting its trajectory as it falls, it is able to home into within a few feet of its designated point of impact.

462
00:39:17,820 --> 00:39:31,820
No site in Iraq was safe as America owned the skies.

463
00:39:33,320 --> 00:39:39,380
In contrast to these high-tech weapons, the MLRS, or Multiple Launched Rocket System,

464
00:39:39,381 --> 00:39:42,780
gave new life to the unguided rocket.

465
00:39:42,781 --> 00:39:47,840
This distant relative of the ancient Chinese rocket depends less on pinpoint accuracy and

466
00:39:47,841 --> 00:39:52,340
more on massive firepower.

467
00:39:52,341 --> 00:39:58,200
The eight inch diameter rockets it fires each carry 600 bomblets in their warhead.

468
00:39:58,201 --> 00:40:02,600
One rocket can cover a football field sized area with instant devastation.

469
00:40:02,601 --> 00:40:09,380
It's a compliment to artillery but it is a counter battery weapon or an interdiction

470
00:40:09,381 --> 00:40:10,380
weapon.

471
00:40:10,381 --> 00:40:13,800
fire rockets over 30 kilometers and cover large areas,

472
00:40:14,520 --> 00:40:17,300
you can knock out an artillery, an enemy battery.

473
00:40:17,860 --> 00:40:19,100
You can knock out the supply area.

474
00:40:19,680 --> 00:40:22,740
You can knock out tanks when they're still in the formation stage

475
00:40:22,741 --> 00:40:23,660
before they make an attack.

476
00:40:28,280 --> 00:40:31,420
But even in this age of high-tech massive firepower,

477
00:40:31,421 --> 00:40:35,660
there is no replacement for the accuracy of hand-placed high explosives.

478
00:40:36,260 --> 00:40:39,780
It is for this role that the Marines of Camp Pendleton train daily.

479
00:40:40,380 --> 00:40:47,380
Today, Charlie Company will attempt to take out a simulated enemy position with high explosives.

480
00:40:47,381 --> 00:40:57,380
There's a bunker, an objective on top of a hill, and we got an assault through some barriers

481
00:40:57,381 --> 00:41:05,380
of Constantino wire and barbed wire and engineer stakes and rough terrain to get to the objective

482
00:41:05,381 --> 00:41:08,380
to take out the objective.

483
00:41:10,380 --> 00:41:15,640
The objective? A hilltop fortification surrounded by trenches and barbed wire.

484
00:41:16,460 --> 00:41:20,560
Bangalore torpedoes, joined sections of pipe filled with high explosives,

485
00:41:20,561 --> 00:41:24,560
are inserted through the barbed wire obstacles under the cover of smoke grenades.

486
00:41:33,540 --> 00:41:40,100
Second squad moves up, laying 40-pound satchel charges to clear the last ramparts of enemy resistance.

487
00:41:40,380 --> 00:41:54,380
Finally, the objective is taken and the exercise complete.

488
00:41:59,100 --> 00:42:02,260
This sort of training paid dividends in Desert Storm,

489
00:42:02,420 --> 00:42:04,820
where the munitions man still had a job to do.

490
00:42:04,821 --> 00:42:12,440
One squad, we go to a bunker and then we would come up real slow first and then we'd check

491
00:42:12,441 --> 00:42:13,820
it out, look inside the bunker.

492
00:42:13,821 --> 00:42:18,660
We'd find any munitions inside the bunker, make sure there isn't any prisoners in there

493
00:42:18,661 --> 00:42:20,080
or any soldiers.

494
00:42:20,081 --> 00:42:24,060
And then we use, sometimes we use grenades, sometimes we use satchel charges.

495
00:42:24,061 --> 00:42:27,780
We'd go in and we'd prime up some explosives and we'd blow it in place.

496
00:42:27,781 --> 00:42:32,820
We'd go from bunker to bunker.

497
00:42:32,821 --> 00:42:46,821
Desert Storm was the zenith of the fast, ultra-accurate delivery of both large and small amounts of chemical explosives.

498
00:42:51,700 --> 00:42:58,740
It was a reminder that large-scale conventional warfare is still a possibility, and one that must be prepared for.

499
00:43:26,600 --> 00:43:27,800
Tuesday Tuesday Tuesday

